# The Omarchy desktop surface, trimmed to what Arch Linux ARM plausibly builds
# for armv7h. Everything here is best effort: the machine still boots and logs
# in without any of it, and whatever pacman cannot resolve is named in
# /var/lib/omarchy/armv7-packages.report to be built from source.
#
# Deliberately absent, because they come from the Omarchy repo
# (pkgs.omarchy.org), which publishes x86_64 only: aether, cliamp, herdr,
# omacalc, omacut, omarchy-nvim, omawrite, tensaku, tobi-try, ttfx. Also absent:
# the x86-only ones (dotnet-runtime, moonlight-qt, gpu-screen-recorder) and the
# heavy builds no RK3288 should attempt (libreoffice-fresh, kdenlive,
# obs-studio). See docs/armv7.md.

hyprland
hyprland-qtutils
uwsm
quickshell
qt6-wayland
qt6-declarative
qt6-imageformats
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-terminal-exec
sddm

foot
nautilus
imv
mpv
mpv-mpris

gnome-keyring
libsecret
gnome-themes-extra
yaru-icon-theme
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd

grim
slurp
wl-clipboard
wtype
